 "researcher_notes": "Passes all legs. Sponsor is Texas Gas Transmission, LLC. The Federal Register notice of 25 March 2015 (FERC docket CP15-105) states 22.5 miles of 24-inch lateral, 230,000 Dth/d, about 81 million dollars, serving a new TVA generating unit at the Paradise Fossil Plant in Muhlenberg County, Kentucky. The EIA pipeline projects release of August 2026 (sheet Historical Projects, Excel row 823) lists it as Completed, in service 26 August 2016, 22.5 miles, 24 inches, 230 MMcf/d, 81 million dollars, docket CP15-105. EIA is one origin; the FERC notice is independent of it. Natural Gas Intelligence also describes the lateral for TVA. Length of about 36 km is above the 25 km floor. Not a match to existing roster: P0263 is the Texas Gas main line, P2518 is the cancelled Clarksville line, P7794 is Borealis. No Western Kentucky lateral row exists. Staged as an expansion-style row under the parent system name as the roster spells it. Start point named from the application and the NGI article; I did not read the full FERC order text. Owner is not in the gazetteer; written in the team style without the comma. Parent company not researched and left blank. Capacity is stated in Dth/d as the notice states it. No route geometry found; official FERC GIS not retrieved, so route is no route and should be sought from the CP15-105 filing."
